  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be two sets such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>X</mi></math> for same set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>. Then,",
    "image": null
